Generate ONLY the PySpark transformation code.
Input DataFrame: `df`. Output DataFrame: `df_transformed`.
Use only: .select(), .withColumn(), .withColumnRenamed(), .cast(), .filter(), .drop()
Use functions from: pyspark.sql.functions (col, lit, trim, lower, to_date, to_timestamp, when, concat_ws, regexp_replace, upper) — anything else is NOT locally verified

CRITICAL RULES:
- String functions WRAP the column: lower(col("f")), trim(col("f")) — never .lower()/.trim() methods
- If forced: substring(col, pos, len) needs int LITERALS; title-case: initcap(col("f")); variable slicing: expr("substring(f, p, length(f))")
- count is imported as spark_count
- Cast only to the mapping's TARGET type: .cast(IntegerType()); dates/timestamps ALWAYS with an explicit format from the hint: to_date(col("f"), "dd-MM-yyyy") — NEVER format-less
- "direct" to a string target = pass through unchanged; add NO casts or cleanups the mappings do not ask for
- No no-ops (self-rename/alias, unchanged re-select); all-direct → df_transformed = df

STRUCTURE (each line converts alone — multi-line calls FAIL):
- ONE .withColumn per statement, one statement per line; first reads df, each next reads df_transformed
- .select() only as a final standalone line with plain string names

Do NOT create classes, helper functions, or imports.
Output ONLY the Python code, no markdown fences.
